    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Stephenville-TX/Talent-Acquisition-Specialist_R-095652-1": {
      "title": "Talent Acquisition Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Talent Acquisition Specialist Agency Tarleton State University Department Talent Acquisition Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Stephenville, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description Tarleton State University, a distinguished Doctoral National Comprehensive University, invites applications for the position of Talent Acquisition Specialist in the Division of Human Resources . As part of a vibrant academic community dedicated to excellence in teaching, research, and service, this role offers the opportunity to contribute meaningfully to a university that values innovation, collaboration, and inclusive growth. Join us in advancing knowledge and transforming lives—on campus and beyond. Tarleton State University continues to grow its impact across Texas, with four distinct campuses located in Stephenville, Fort Worth, RELLIS-Bryan and Waco , along with a robust online community that extends our reach even further. At the heart of it all is Stephenville , where Tarleton State offers a dynamic environment for faculty and staff. From a lively live music scene and numerous local festivals to rich traditions rooted in the surrounding community, Stephenville provides a vibrant and welcoming atmosphere. No matter where you're located—on campus or online—you are part of a mission that transforms lives and makes a difference across the state of Texas and beyond. ________________________________________________________________________ Important Immigration Information: A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Please be advised that Tarleton State University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to ascertain whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Tarleton State University subject to this fee.     In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate.  ________________________________________________________________________ The Talent Acquisition Specialist, under general supervision, performs routine and complex specialized human resources duties in support of talent acquisition, hiring operations, and position management activities. The Talent Acquisition Specialist provides consultative and operational support to hiring managers, departments, and HR partners throughout the recruitment and hiring process. Responsibilities include supporting full-cycle recruitment, job description consultation, candidate screening, hiring workflow coordination, pre-employment processing, and related HR activities while ensuring compliance with university policies and applicable state and federal laws and regulations. The position also assists in compiling reports, maintaining records, improving processes, and supporting the development and implementation of human resources procedures and forms. The role currently operates in a broad capacity that includes recruitment planning, sourcing, candidate screening, hiring manager consultation, job description and position management support, compensation-related hiring support, offer coordination, pre-employment processing, and monitoring hiring activity in Workday. The incumbent also supports shared Talent Acquisition operations by tracking approvals, managing communication channels, and responding to general hiring-related inquiries. As the Talent Acquisition function continues to evolve, this position is expected to shift toward a more specialized recruiting model with increased emphasis on proactive sourcing, talent pipeline development, hiring manager consultation, and recruitment strategy, while continuing to promote consistency, efficiency, compliance, and a positive candidate and hiring manager experience. No visa sponsorship is available for this role. This position is in Stephenville, Texas with work hours of Monday–Friday, 8am–5pm, or as work requirements indicate; which may include afterhours and some weekends during peak periods. Responsibilities Serves to provide consultative and operational support to hiring managers, department representatives, and HR partners throughout the recruitment and hiring process. Supports full-cycle recruitment activities, including intake discussions, sourcing, job postings, candidate screening, interview coordination, candidate communication, offer preparation, and pre-employment processing. Develops and implements recruitment strategies to attract qualified candidates using job boards, professional networks, recruiting platforms, and other sourcing channels. Reviews applications and candidate materials to assess qualifications and support hiring recommendations based on established position requirements. Consults with hiring managers and HR partners on job descriptions, position requirements, minimum qualifications, and related hiring documentation. Supports foundational position management activities by assisting with position description updates, position-related documentation, and review of position data for accuracy and alignment with institutional standards. Provides preliminary compensation-related hiring support by evaluating candidate qualifications in relation to approved hiring ranges and institutional guidance, in collaboration with appropriate HR stakeholders. Prepares, processes, and coordinates employment offers, background checks, I-9 requirements, and other pre-hire actions to support timely onboarding. Reviews, enters, monitors, and follows up on actions in Workday or related HR systems, including hiring transactions, approvals, workflow progress, and related documentation. Assists in managing recruitment records, reports, and documents related to talent acquisition and hiring activities. Responds to and assists with HR-related questions from hiring managers, employees, applicants, and campus stakeholders, providing guidance on recruitment processes, timelines, policies, and next steps. Provides guidance to departments regarding HR practices, compliance requirements, applicable laws and regulations, and ethical hiring practices. Assists in planning, developing, revising, and implementing HR procedures, forms, and standard operating procedures related to talent acquisition and hiring operations. Compiles and prepares reports, surveys, and related documentation regarding recruitment and hiring activities, and may conduct studies or recommend process improvements based on identified needs. Supports shared Talent Acquisition operations, including monitoring communication channels, routing inquiries, and helping maintain continuity of service during periods of high volume or staffing transition. May coordinate, plan, and provide logistical support for recruitment events, outreach activities, training sessions, and other specialized HR programs. May cross train on other specialized human resources functions to support operational needs and service continuity. Attends HR training and informational meetings and remains informed on relevant recruiting practices, employment regulations, and process changes. Performs other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications Required Education and Experience Bachelor’s Degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, or closely related field. Equivalent combination of relevant education and experience may be substituted as appropriate. Two years of direct experience in talent acquisition, with emphasis on recruiting, sourcing, and candidate pipeline development. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge of full-cycle recruitment practices, sourcing methods, and candidate screening and evaluation techniques. Knowledge of applicable laws, regulations, policies, and best practices related to hiring, recruitment, and employment processes. Strong verbal and written communication skills with the ability to communicate clearly, professionally, and effectively with candidates, hiring managers, and university stakeholders. Strong interpersonal, customer service, and relationship-building skills with the ability to provide guidance and support throughout the hiring process. Ability to work independently, take initiative, and manage multiple priorities with attention to accuracy and deadlines. Strong organizational and time management skills with the ability to coordinate and support multiple concurrent hiring activities. Ability to review, interpret, verify, and maintain accurate data, records, and documentation across multiple systems and formats. Ability to identify, research, and resolve routine and moderately complex process, system, and workflow issues. Skill in using applicant tracking systems, HR systems, Microsoft Office Suite, and other related software. Familiarity with social media, recruiting platforms, candidate databases, and professional networks used for sourcing and outreach. Ability to document procedures, support standard operating procedure updates, and contribute to process improvement efforts. Ability to maintain confidentiality, exercise sound judgment, and handle sensitive information appropriately. Ability to work effectively both independently and collaboratively as part of a team. Preferred Qualifications Experience serving as a recruiting partner with responsibility for consultative hiring manager support and full-cycle recruitment. Experience using Workday or another applicant tracking system to manage recruitment workflows and hiring transactions. Experience developing sourcing strategies and proactively building candidate pipelines for a variety of roles. Experience using job boards, social media, professional networks, and other recruiting tools to identify and engage talent. Experience conducting candidate screenings and supporting interview and selection processes. Experience in higher education, public sector, or another complex, policy-driven environment. Familiarity with job description review, position-related documentation, or compensation-related hiring support. The responsibilities outlined above represent the core functions of this position and are not intended to serve as a comprehensive list of all duties performed. Standard operating procedures associated with these functions will be developed and maintained as needed.   Compensation & Benefits Salary: Commensurate with experience Salary Range: The target base annual salary range is $49,000 up to $59,119 and may be negotiable based on funding availability and candidate experience/skillset in relation to the minimum requirements of this position. We are proud to offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time and qualifying part-time employees. Our Careers Page   offers an overview of the great benefits we offer; for detailed information visit our Benefits Information page. Qualified candidates are encouraged to submit a completed application for consideration. Initial review of applications will begin immediately and continue until position is filled. Application Procedure: During the application process applicants have one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents and Submit the application. Applicants will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once the application materials have been submitted via \"Submit\" action. Employment applications must include: Completed online application Cover Letter / Letter of Interest addressing qualifications Curriculum Vitae or Resume At least 3 current professional references and their full contact information Applications received by Tarleton State University must have all job application data entered.  Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application.  “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application.  Incomplete applications will not be considered. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Stephenville-TX/Events-Coordinator_R-095344-1": {
      "title": "Events Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Events Coordinator Agency Tarleton State University Department Event Services Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Stephenville, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description Tarleton State University, a distinguished Doctoral National Comprehensive University, invites applications for the position of Events Coordinator in the Department of Event Services . As part of a vibrant academic community dedicated to excellence in teaching, research, and service, this role offers the opportunity to contribute meaningfully to a university that values innovation, collaboration, and inclusive growth. Join us in advancing knowledge and transforming lives—on campus and beyond. Tarleton State University continues to grow its impact across Texas, with four distinct campuses located in Stephenville, Fort Worth, RELLIS-Bryan and Waco , along with a robust online community that extends our reach even further. At the heart of it all is Stephenville , where Tarleton State offers a dynamic environment for faculty and staff. From a lively live music scene and numerous local festivals to rich traditions rooted in the surrounding community, Stephenville provides a vibrant and welcoming atmosphere. No matter where you're located—on campus or online—you are part of a mission that transforms lives and makes a difference across the state of Texas and beyond. ________________________________________________________________________ Important Immigration Information: A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Please be advised that Tarleton State University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to ascertain whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Tarleton State University subject to this fee.     In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate.  ________________________________________________________________________ The Events Coordinator serves as an event representative and planner to support special university sponsored events. Coordinates and makes special arrangements for various high-level special events. Assist with all phases of event development, including event planning and event team coordination, and assist with providing deliverables to help drive projects to a successful completion. Work hours: Mon-Fri; 8 AM-5 PM or as work requirements indicate. Primary location will be on-site at Tarleton State University's Stephenville campus. Travel required to multiple work site locations. Responsibilities: Coordinates and markets large events and conferences. Schedules and processes event requests developing service requirements and arranging logistics. Prepares correspondence, reports, purchase orders, and invoices related to special events. Provides on-site customer liaison during events. Coordinates post-event review and follow-up contact. Participates in the supervision of ambassador student organization. Assists with researching and cultivating networking opportunities.   Acts as representative of Campus Operations and as valued member of Tarleton State as part of The Texas A&M system and performs other duties as assigned, including serving satellite campuses. Minimum Qualifications Required Education and Experience: Bachelor’s degree in applicable field or equivalent combination of education and experience. Three years of related experience. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Exceptional problem-solving, critical thinking, and time management skills. Capability to handle confidential and sensitive information with discretion. Ability to multitask and work cooperatively with others. Strong organizational skills. Effective verbal and written communication skills. Knowledge of word processing and spreadsheet applications. Ability to be accountable, responsible, and dependable member of the Campus Operations team. Ability to work flexible hours and extended schedule to support events and duties that take place outside the normal operating hours. Compensation & Benefits Salary: Commensurate with experience Salary Range: The target base annual salary range is $41,000 up to $45,100 and may be negotiable based on funding availability and candidate experience/skillset in relation to the minimum requirements of this position. We are proud to offer a comprehensive benefits package for full-time and qualifying part-time employees. Our Careers Page   offers an overview of the great benefits we offer; for detailed information visit our Benefits Information page. Qualified candidates are encouraged to submit a completed application for consideration. Initial review of applications will begin immediately and continue until position is filled. Application Procedure: During the application process applicants have one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents and Submit the application. Applicants will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once the application materials have been submitted via \"Submit\" action. Employment applications must include: Completed online application Cover Letter / Letter of Interest addressing qualifications Curriculum Vitae or Resume At least 3 current professional references and their full contact information Applications received by Tarleton State University must have all job application data entered.  Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application.  “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application.  Incomplete applications will not be considered. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Stephenville-TX/Guest-Service-Event-Worker_R-085968-2": {
      "title": "Guest Service Event Worker - Part Time",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Title Guest Service Event Worker - Part Time Agency Tarleton State University Department Event Center Guest Services Proposed Minimum Salary $18.03 hourly Job Location Stephenville, Texas Job Type Temporary/Casual Staff (Fixed Term) Job Description Tarleton State University, a distinguished Doctoral National Comprehensive University, invites applications for the position of part time Guest Service Event Workers in the Department of Event Services . As part of a vibrant academic community dedicated to excellence in teaching, research, and service, this role offers the opportunity to contribute meaningfully to a university that values innovation, collaboration, and inclusive growth. Join us in advancing knowledge and transforming lives—on campus and beyond. Tarleton State University continues to grow its impact across Texas, with four distinct campuses located in Stephenville, Fort Worth, RELLIS-Bryan and Waco , along with a robust online community that extends our reach even further. At the heart of it all is Stephenville , where Tarleton State offers a dynamic environment for faculty and staff. From a lively live music scene and numerous local festivals to rich traditions rooted in the surrounding community, Stephenville provides a vibrant and welcoming atmosphere. No matter where you're located—on campus or online—you are part of a mission that transforms lives and makes a difference across the state of Texas and beyond. ________________________________________________________________________ Important Immigration Information: A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Please be advised that Tarleton State University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to ascertain whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Tarleton State University subject to this fee.     In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate.  ________________________________________________________________________ The Event Services Worker plays a key role in supporting the Tarleton State University Event Center by delivering exceptional front-line customer service and ensuring smooth event operations. Core responsibilities include ushering at events, assisting with ticket sales and entry, monitoring building security, and maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment. This position is essential to creating a positive and seamless experience for guests, students, and community members. Strong communication, teamwork, and problem-solving skills are critical to success in this role. Evening and weekend availability is required, with work schedules determined by the needs of scheduled events. This is a temporary, part-time position limited to a maximum of 19 hours per week, based on the operational needs of the Event Center. Job Duties/Responsibilities: Provide service as an usher for campus wide events such as concerts, athletic events, etc. Event ticket sales support as needed Scanning tickets at University events Perform building operation tasks including locking and unlocking main doors, various offices, etc. Provide front line customer service including answering phones, transferring calls, giving directions, and assisting patrons and general public Monitor building security as needed Reporting building maintenance, cleaning, and safety concerns Maintain a clean and organized workspace Work with other building staff team members to solve problems, provide updated information, and assist with scheduling as needed Coordinate evacuation procedures in the case of an emergency Assist with filling shifts and special event needs Provide other duties as assigned Required Qualifications: Customer service experience Must be available to work nights and weekends Preferred Qualifications: Common business software applications such as Microsoft Office Familiar with audio and visual and presentation equipment Experience serving as a student leader in a professional environment Skills/Abilities: Problem solving Lift, carry and/or otherwise move items weighing up to approximately 20 pounds on occasion Ability to move about and between venues for extended periods of time up to a full shift of work Bend and stoop Compensation :   The target base hourly compensation is $18.03 and may be negotiable based on funding availability and candidate experience/skillset in relation to the minimum requirements of this position. Applications received by Tarleton State University must have all job application data entered.  Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application.  “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application.  Incomplete applications will not be considered.   All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Stephenville-TX/Clinical-Assistant-Associate-Professor-and-CHCP-Director-of-Simulation-Education_R-095468-1": {
      "title": "Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor and CHCP Director of Simulation Education",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor and CHCP Director of Simulation Education Agency Tarleton State University Department College of Health & Clinical Professions Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location Stephenville, Texas Job Type Faculty Job Description Tarleton State University, a distinguished Doctoral National Comprehensive University, invites applications for the position of Clinical Assistant/Associate Professor and Director of Simulation Education in the College of Health and Clinical Professions . As part of a vibrant academic community dedicated to excellence in teaching, research, and service, this role offers the opportunity to contribute meaningfully to a university that values innovation, collaboration, and inclusive growth. Join us in advancing knowledge and transforming lives—on campus and beyond. Tarleton State University continues to grow its impact across Texas, with four distinct campuses located in Stephenville, Fort Worth, RELLIS-Bryan and Waco , along with a robust online community that extends our reach even further. At the heart of it all is Stephenville , where Tarleton State offers a dynamic environment for faculty and staff. From a lively live music scene and numerous local festivals to rich traditions rooted in the surrounding community, Stephenville provides a vibrant and welcoming atmosphere. No matter where you're located—on campus or online—you are part of a mission that transforms lives and makes a difference across the state of Texas and beyond. ________________________________________________________________________ Important Immigration Information: A Presidential proclamation issued on September 19, 2025, imposes a $100,000 fee on new H-1B petitions filed after September 21, 2025. Please be advised that Tarleton State University will NOT pay this fee. Therefore, if you need immigration sponsorship for your employment, we recommend that you consult with your private immigration counsel at your own expense to ascertain whether your current immigration status would make a potential offer of employment from Tarleton State University subject to this fee.     In addition, on January 27, 2026, Texas Governor Abbot issued a moratorium on the filing of any new H-1B unless approved by the Texas Workforce Commission. Accordingly, if you will now or in the future require sponsorship for employment visa status this moratorium may affect our ability to employ you should you be selected as the final candidate.  ________________________________________________________________________ This is a 12-month, clinical-track position located on Tarleton State University's main campus in Stephenville, Texas. Work hours: Monday-Friday; 8:00 AM-5:00 PM or as work and teaching requirements indicate. May be assigned to teach at various campus locations or through approved instructional modalities, as determined by the institution based on operational needs. Serves as a Campus Security Authority (CSA) as defined by the Clery Act. The faculty member will be expected to demonstrate excellence and innovation in teaching, maintain professional engagement within the discipline, mentor graduate students, and participate in the necessary operation and accreditation activities of the Clinical Graduate Simulation Education Program and the institution. Essential Duties and Responsibilities 80% Teaching and Service: Plan, prepare, and deliver graduate lectures, laboratories, seminars, and simulation education activities within the College of Health and Clinical Professions. Develop course syllabi, instructional materials, laboratory exercises, examinations, and assessment tools. Assess student performance, provide timely feedback, and evaluate student learning outcomes for continuous program improvement. Engage students in active learning, critical thinking, and hands-on simulation laboratory experiences consistent with professional standards. Provide academic advising, mentoring, and career guidance to prospective and current students. Participate in student recruitment, retention, progression, and graduation initiatives. Maintain compliance with university policies, academic standards, and accreditation requirements. Collaborate with faculty, clinical affiliates, and university personnel to ensure effective program delivery. Participate in departmental, college, university, and professional service activities, including committee assignments and faculty governance. Maintain professional credentials, certifications, and continuing education activities relevant to Clinical Graduate Simulation Education. 20% Administrative: As Director of Simulation Education, the faculty member will: Provide leadership, oversight, and administration of the Simulation Education. Ensure ongoing compliance with all accreditation standards of each program in the College of Health and Clinical Professions. Coordinate preparation and submission of accreditation reports, annual updates, self-studies, and substantive change documentation. Lead curriculum development, review, assessment, and continuous quality improvement activities. Coordinate program assessment plans and student learning outcome evaluations. Serve as the primary point of contact for students regarding academic progression and professional development. Develop and maintain relationships with affiliated clinical education sites throughout Texas and other approved locations. Monitor and evaluate simulation education effectiveness. Collaborate with the Department Head, Program Director, faculty, and staff regarding scheduling and strategic planning. Assist with faculty recruitment, mentoring, and onboarding related to program needs. Support the development of articulation pathways and opportunities. Represent the Program at professional meetings, recruitment events, advisory board meetings, and accreditation activities. Maintain records and documentation necessary for program operations and accreditation compliance. Summer Appointment: Teaching/Service Teaching assignments are determined by the Dean and Program Directors based on program needs. Admin assignments as determined by the Dean and Program Director based on program needs. Minimum Requirements Required Education and Experience: Doctoral degree (PhD, EdD, or equivalent) in a relevant field, OR Master's degree in a health-related field with significant simulation education experience from an accredited university. Additional certification in simulation education preferred (e.g., CHSE, CHSOS) or equivalent professional credential. Eligibility to serve as Director under current ARC-PA and CAPTE accreditation standards. Excellent written and oral communication skills in English. Required Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Knowledge and understanding of Clinical Graduate Simulation Education, accreditation standards, curriculum development, clinical education requirements, and assessment practices; ability to lead and administer an accredited academic program; ability to establish and maintain effective relationships with students, faculty, staff, clinical affiliates, and professional organizations; strong organizational, communication, and leadership skills; ability to interact with students, staff, and faculty in a professional, collegial, and collaborative manner. ***Compensation will be competitive and commensurate with experience***   Application Procedure: During the application process applicants have one opportunity to enter the requested information, upload documents, and Submit the application. Applicants will not be able to make changes or add additional documents once the application materials have been submitted via the \"Submit\" action. Employment applications must include (required): Completed online application Cover Letter / Letter of Interest addressing qualifications Curriculum Vitae or Resume At least 3 current professional references and their full contact information Unofficial transcripts Applicants with degrees earned outside the United States must submit transcripts translated into English, along with an official credential evaluation from a recognized service. Philosophy Statement related to Teaching and utilizing the simulation laboratory Applications received by Tarleton State University must have all job application data entered. Failure to provide all job application data could result in an invalid submission and a rejected application. “See resume” is not an acceptable entry in the job application. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Anticipated start date Fall 2026. Official transcripts must be received directly from each degree‐granting institution prior to a letter of appointment being issued. All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
